observed = "formerly observation.6.11.terminal-authenticated-discriminator. Both supplied native artifacts, /root/lx-lanes/native/qual-logs/item5-executed-native.json and /root/lx-lanes/native/platform/sdk/conformance/fixtures/receipt-programs-executed-v3.json, pass receipt signature, activity-id binding and terminal/call-graph digest checks. Authenticated protocol/module/guest-ABI/runtime versions are 3/4/2/1. The receipt binds outcome encoding, terminal kind/result, runtime/ABI, fee/metering versions and usage, occupancy commitments, transfer root, terminal root and graph root. Its CALL_OUTCOME event additionally binds program, principal, activity, frame and event-envelope digest (src/modules/programs/event.c:197-236); it does not carry transfer legs or transfer-set version. execution-v4 binds runtime, fee/metering versions, outputs, usage, optional trace, program, guest ABI, result/response and graph (execute.rs:2072-2152). Graph evidence binds principal, graph limits and caller/callee/depth edges (calls.rs:356-375), not capability sets or transfer sources. Guest ABI2 produces both transfer-set versions: transfer.rs:330-341 selects V2 from root ProgramSpend, nested ProgramSpend, or Program/ProgramFunding sources. abi/capability.rs:519-536 permits caller-owned ProgramSpend to originate on an edge; absence of root ProgramSpend alone cannot classify all nested executions. The activity-id-bound native call supplies guest ABI and root capability grants, but those bytes are absent from the standalone terminal decoder inputs. In these artifacts its sole Transfer402 grant has maximum_amount 1. Permission maxima are not general applied-leg evidence. The candidate response is empty, graph length is 86, receipt amount is zero, and its sole effect is the CALL_OUTCOME event. No existing receipt or terminal field independently identifies transfer-set V1 versus V2 without the authority attachment, and no applied principal leg list is supplied for canonical_kernel_legs/root reconstruction (transfer.rs:1183-1230)."
