observed = "formerly observation.6.8.topology-model-and-existing-parser-limit. The checker now applies the supplied namespace only to documents without metadata.namespace, includes developer/internal manifests by default, follows ExternalName DNS chains without remapping the requested port, and checks DNS policy peers against kube-system/kube-dns labels. python3 qual-logs/au28/topology-regressions.py exits 1 in qual-logs/au28/topology-regressions-all.log: the current PyYAML model passes the 40 existing edges and retains the two missing Human failures; nine negative mutations detect alias cycles, missing/off-cluster alias targets, wrong target Service ports, selectors selecting no workload, invalid targetPort names, denied ingress, denied egress and denied DNS; explicit namespace precedence and the developer apply namespace pass. Full-parser parity remains failed: the built-in parser reports line 69 was not consumed for the node manifest. Running the unchanged HEAD checker and node manifest with bash qual-logs/au28/topology-baseline.sh --yaml-parser builtin qual-logs/au28/node-baseline.yaml also exits 1 with the same error in qual-logs/au28/builtin-baseline.log."
assumption = "The built-in parser defect precedes these changes and is recorded without altering its assertion or broadening the parser repair. This is static topology evidence, not pod connectivity or first-payment proof. cg spec lint exits 0 with zero errors and nine existing warnings in qual-logs/au28/spec-lint.log. git diff --check exits 0 in qual-logs/au28/diff-check.log. No spec task status changes or passing full-task gate are claimed."
severity = "blocker"

[observation.6.8.93]
task = "6.8"
file = "platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh platform/hosted/node/deployment.yaml platform/hosted/agent-boundary/src/main.rs platform/hosted/internal/src/events.rs platform/hosted/webhooks/src/trusted.rs"
symbol = "developer-component.token LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_GATEWAY_TOKEN_FILE LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_REGISTRY_TOKEN_FILE observe"
observed = "formerly observation.6.8.developer-component-token-and-observation-producer. The bring-up generates developer-component.token and mounts it for webhooks, while node/deployment.yaml:204-205 supplies only the distinct gateway and registry component credentials that agent-boundary/src/main.rs:428-429 loads and :1668,1676 authenticates. The webhook ReceiptVerifier calls that component in trusted.rs:459-488; admitting its network edge does not authorize its separate bearer. The internal event source requires authenticated POST /internal/v1/observe at events.rs:256 to capture a resource snapshot and bind it to its principal before serving an immutable event; bringing up its Deployment alone does not provide an observation/trigger producer."
assumption = "A dedicated webhook component credential contract and a real event observation/trigger integration need changes beyond the owned cluster-script and policy repair. No gateway or registry credential is reassigned to webhooks, no authentication check is weakened and no observation is fabricated. NEEDS.md contains the exact follow-up requests."
severity = "blocker"

[observation.6.9.2]
