observed = "formerly observation.3.6.emulator-occupancy-batch-finalization. LXP_ERR_PROGRAM_REFUSED is -736 and LXP_ERR_NON_CANONICAL is -3 in include/layerx/lxp_result.h. ffi_call.rs emits callback stage 5 when settle_call_occupancy refuses. Temporary diagnostic instrumentation at its prepare_batch error mapping produced verbatim: occupancy prepare batch=4: BatchRegression { previous: 1, attempted: 4 }. cargo test --locked --manifest-path platform/Cargo.toml -p layerx-platform-emulator --test gateway lifecycle_routes_execute_and_replay_real_native_state_receipts -- --nocapture exits 101 (qual-logs/r16/occupancy-diagnosis.log). The unchanged ledger check requires batch == last_finalized_batch + 1. Activity settlement does not finalize the batch. The emulator called lxp_kernel_execute_activity and incremented batch_number without occupancy maintenance, leaving the ledger anchored at batch 1 when the second call attempted batch 4. The native post_upgrade_maintenance_case reuses the identical call payload after upgrade, but publish_artifact_fixture_batch invokes lxp_kernel_prepare_batch_maintenance after each activity. No capability or program-version rebinding is needed."
assumption = "The refusal correctly protects consecutive occupancy settlement; the defect is the emulator coordinator omitting required maintenance. platform_emulator_execute now invokes the same lxp_programs_finalize_occupancy_batch_selected kernel routine used by prepared batch maintenance, with the selected fee schedule, batch, timestamp, parameter version and next global sequence. It publishes the real maintenance receipt through the bound state-feed observer and takes its next global sequence from committed state. Original activity receipts and all success assertions remain intact. Added lifecycle assertions prove activity sequences 1,3,5,7,9 and one maintenance sequence per batch across replay and snapshot restoration. Temporary Rust diagnostics are removed; no runtime or kernel check changes remain."
severity = "note"

