symbol = "leaf_set lxp_state_root balance_leaf verify_balance_proof CheckpointProof::encode_publication"
observed = "Native replay commits module-keyed composite state with LXP/v1/state-leaf and LXP/v1/state-node domains and explicit key/value lengths. Settlement balance and withdrawal publication require flat LXP/v1/merkle-leaf and LXP/v1/merkle-node paths equal to that registered resulting state root. The canonical publication proof carries only a leaf index and siblings, with no native subtree or composite-state proof layers. ExitEvidence::encode_publication and CheckpointProof::encode_publication enforce this incompatible root equality before publication. Existing native paths therefore cannot construct the requested nonempty settlement witnesses against real replayed batch roots."
assumption = "A protocol-authorized proof representation or separate committed settlement root must be supplied by the state and settlement verifier owners. Native roots, claim verifiers and publication assertions remain intact. Publishing empty vectors for existing balances or synthetic checkpoint roots would not satisfy replay-derived settlement evidence. Settlement publication and its extended consumer-fetch integration remain unimplemented."
severity = "blocker"

