symbol = "execute_withdrawal"
observed = "The asset module advertises WITHDRAW at ordinal 9. Its exact 108-byte payload contains asset, u128 amount, 20-byte recipient, request anchor and u64 fee limit. Module validation verifies the signed activity and payload hash, binds the account authority and actor, requires the signed fee limit to match the envelope, and executes the existing withdrawal request path with owner transfer authority. The canonical record uses the activity ID as withdrawal ID and preserves the request anchor and nullifier domain. Eighteen real module-dispatch cases cover success, signature and payload tampering, absent and mismatched authority, fee mismatch and overflow, sequence, balance, asset, pause, freeze, zero amount, zero recipient, zero anchor and exact payload length; repeated signed requests are refused against committed KV. Successful execution proves the strict-decoded withdrawal record against the composite root. make -j16, make test-asset-withdraw-activity test-asset-registry test-asset-withdraw test-state-proof, the additional negative-case target, the focused Rust state_proof test, forge fmt --check, forge build and forge test exit 0. All 149 Solidity tests pass. Logs and exit files are under qual-logs/set1, including withdraw-activity-build, withdraw-activity-final, withdraw-activity-negative, rust-state-proof and forge-test. Native vectors were regenerated because the registered module activity table is part of the composite commitment."
assumption = "This qualifies the native module path, not WITHDRAW admission or replay through the daemon. cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_process.c and cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_lni.c explicitly recognize SEND and were outside this settlement implementation. Admission, authority-scope, ABI-selection and replay changes are required there. The invocation-local withdrawal store retains the existing type and request API; committed KV supplies durable duplicate detection. The aggregate guarantor invocation initially exits 2 for missing eth_abi; it does not qualify daemon replay."
severity = "blocker"

