observed = "Identity creation requires and echoes a bounded tenant and preserves the checked request/response binding. Real identity service tests and all-targets Clippy pass. Treasury and sequencer account provisioning calls the existing protocol account derivation. The evidence assembler stages the complete protected file set and journal before publication. The Job uses the runtime identity PVC and validates receipt inclusion under the first-batch sequencer pin. The retained real native second-batch receipt is independently verified and refused for fresh limits. The generated catalog loads through PurposePresetCatalog's public re-export. Locked provider build, all-targets Clippy and tests including layerx-human-service pass, as do twelve provisioning tests, four existing material tests, formatting, shell syntax and beta-ledger-check. Exact commands, exit codes and logs are recorded in qual-logs/hm9/hm9e-gates.json."
assumption = "Local source qualification does not resolve observations 6.8.89 through 6.8.91. No complete generated evidence set, positive first-batch live acceptance, Kubernetes Job, image or cluster qualification is claimed."

[observation.3.4.6]
task = "3.4"
severity = "blocker"
file = "programs/crates/layerx-programs-registry/src/protocol_evidence.rs cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_process.c cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_deployment.inc platform/hosted/registry/tests/native_deployment.rs"
symbol = "DeploymentProof ProgramStateProof ProtocolDeploymentVerifier::verify_receipt decode_trust_history lxp_daemon_deployment_encode"
observed = "Real protocol-3 deployment through a fresh layerxd LNI produces a signed deployment receipt at sequence 1 in a two-receipt batch ending at sequence 2. Rust inclusion verification of the retained receipt and signed header passes; their resulting state roots differ after occupancy maintenance. The deployment proof selector refuses -903 because the live Programs root cannot be bound to the earlier deployment receipt root. Both positive native-deployment and journal-pair tests fail without changing their assertions. Separately, decode_trust_history only accepts protocol versions 1 and 2. Evidence: qual-logs/reg2/cargo-test.log and qual-logs/reg2/native-proof-test.log."
assumption = "An explicitly versioned maintained-batch DeploymentProof is required in the Programs registry crate: retain the deployment receipt, authenticate the maintenance receipt and both inclusion paths under the signed header, and bind Programs and lifecycle witnesses to the maintained root through the existing maintained-outcome verifier. Legacy equality checks must remain intact. The Programs verifier is outside the permitted implementation paths; no journal pair or complete deployment qualification is claimed."

[observation.3.4.7]
task = "3.4"
severity = "blocker"
file = "platform/hosted/registry/deployment.yaml platform/hosted/agent-boundary/src/main.rs platform/hosted/human/provision.sh platform/hosted/tests/beta-cluster.sh"
symbol = "LAYERX_REGISTRY_LNI_SOCKET LAYERX_REGISTRY_JOURNAL human_evidence_provision"
observed = "The registry StatefulSet occupies a separate pod without the node LNI socket. The authenticated node endpoint is the agent boundary, whose forwarding policy only exposes selected routes. The Human evidence function invokes a host-local assembler with a journal path; no human-evidence Job exists in the merged checkout. The registry implementation exports legacy canonical admission/deployment bytes to its journal pairs subdirectory only after verified envelope publication. No cluster script change or cluster execution was performed because the granted volume-and-environment-only edit cannot establish the absent transport and host export contract."
assumption = "Hosted activation requires an authenticated selector-4 bridge or supported LNI transport and peer policy, plus a defined shared-volume or host-export path for the Human assembler. These require changes outside the registry and native daemon ownership or a supplied integration contract. No fabricated receipts, synthetic proofs, protocol-version fallback, cluster gate, image gate, push or PR is claimed."

[observation.6.1.92]
task = "6.1"
file = "cmd/layerx-guarantor/runtime.c cmd/layerx-guarantor/settlement.py platform/hosted/node/deployment.yaml docs/wiki/Guarantor.md"
symbol = "gp_runtime_open gp_runtime_oracle membership"
observed = "formerly observation.6.1.34. The independent runtime verifies genesis and executes real kernel transitions without the sequencer private key. Direct owner authority matches the node adapter. Nonempty oracle inputs and rotated signer histories lacking complete authorization reconstruction refuse explicitly. The deployed topology provisions two distinct signing identities, two mutual-TLS processes and a dedicated checkpoint submitter, but both guarantors share the cluster operator and provide no operational independence. Certificates carry empty validity proofs and use implemented v2 domain tags."
