symbol = "encode_trust_history human_journal_deploy beta_cluster_up"
observed = "Bring-up now applies and waits for the registry before sending human-evidence-input/program-deployment.lxa as application/octet-stream to its real authenticated deployment ingress with server-name verification, client certificate and request bearer. It requires HTTP 200 deployed state and the response receipt-digest pair in the exported journal before human_evidence_provision. Shell syntax, embedded Python syntax, execution-order assertions, missing-input refusal before cluster access and eighteen Human Python tests pass. Logs: qual-logs/reg2/reg2d-order-shell.log, reg2d-order-static.log, reg2d-order-missing-input.log and reg2d-order-human.log. No program-deployment.lxa producer exists in this bring-up. encode_trust_history emits version 2 and sequencer-pins.py explicitly asserts version 2, whereas the node bootstraps protocol 3."
assumption = "A real signed NativeProgramDeploy activity with current account sequence, valid deployable artifact and funded signing authority must be supplied by its owner at the protected input path; no signed activity, admission or receipt is fabricated. Trust-history generation and the pin assertion require coordinated protocol-3 reconciliation outside the execution-order-only script grant. Registry verification remains intact and refuses incompatible trust. Cluster startup, ingress deployment and mounted-volume export were not run because Docker, kubectl and kind are unavailable. These local checks do not close the full ingress qualification gap."

