symbol = "register _validateHeader"
observed = "Both real producers attest batch 1; eth_call of the identical registration calldata and eth_estimateGas return code 3, data 0xbabb01dd, decoded as InvalidHeader(). Header timestamp 1788951381618 milliseconds exceeds disposable block timestamp 172809 seconds times 1000 plus the unchanged 60000 millisecond future-drift bound. Protocol 3, network 77, epoch 1, batch 1, sequences 1..2, initial finalized fields zero, nonzero roots and previous-state-root equality all satisfy the remaining header preconditions. Membership, threshold and signature validation already pass in register. The disposable harness now advances its own chain 31337 to wall time after real timelock setup, mines and asserts the observed timestamp."
assumption = "This repairs task-scoped disposable clock setup without changing contract bounds, native timestamps, attestations or assertions. The full producer and owner harness do not exist at base 21c96f47. A focused real-contract comparison runs first at that scratch base and then current source: both reject future timestamps through eth_call and estimation, accept identical calldata after clock alignment and register a real bonded certificate. Both comparison commands exit 0; logs and reproducible probe: qual-logs/own1/own1f-base-settlement.log, own1f-current-settlement.log, own1f-settlement-compare.py. Original live revert evidence: own1f-checkpoint-preconditions.log. Temporary RPC instrumentation is not part of the implementation. Final-source real custody/Governance lifecycle/restart exits 0 (own1f-final-lifecycle.log), Python provider suite passes 27 tests (own1f-python.log), and the final checkpoint command exits 1 after batch 1 registers and batch 2 refuses (own1f-final-checkpoint.log)."

[observation.3.7.53]
task = "3.7"
severity = "blocker"
file = "contracts/CheckpointRegistry.sol cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_process.c cmd/layerx-guarantor/settlement.py tests/daemon/owner_checkpoint.py"
symbol = "_validateHeader registerCheckpoint checkpoint"
observed = "After clock alignment the real owner flow registers batch 1 and both producers attest batch 2. eth_call of the exact batch-2 registration calldata and eth_estimateGas return InvalidHeader(), code 3/data 0xbabb01dd. Batch 2 has epoch 1 while finalisedEpoch is 1; contract line 341 rejects header.epoch <= finalisedEpoch. Batch 2 and firstSequence 3 follow finalisedBatchNumber 1 and finalisedLastSequence 2; lastSequence is 4, timestamp increases and is within the wall-clock bound, and previousStateRoot equals latestFinalisedStateRoot. Both base and current separately deployed contracts also reject a real signed contiguous same-epoch successor. Contract source is unchanged from 21c96f47. Raw live preconditions: qual-logs/own1/own1f-clock-fixed-diagnostic.log."
assumption = "The settlement contract precondition conflicts with native multiple-batches-per-epoch behavior: seal uses kernel.epoch and retained replay rejects decreasing epochs, not equal epochs. The settlement implementation must reconcile epoch progression while preserving exact next-batch, next-sequence, timestamp, root, bond and certificate checks. No contract or signed-header change is made here. Full owner checkpoint qualification remains blocked at batch 2; hosted positive finality queries remain unreached."

