observed = "Asset ordinals 1, 4, 6, 7, 8, 10 and 11 retain fee-parameter version 1 and the existing complete-activity-type, byte, execution and storage formula with the existing multiplier rounding. Admission, replay and refusal policy remains unchanged. Exact computed fees for every new ordinal, genesis snapshot registration and reserved ordinal refusal, and independent kernel replay with guarantor root recomputation across eight batches pass. Each new ordinal produces a verified signed replay receipt; mutated resulting roots are refused. Account enumeration uses LNI request tag 7 kind 3 with derived DID id32, latest selector and rank at most 3; response tag 8 carries sorted account values with individual account proofs and refuses response overflow. The schema now describes this existing route. make test-fees test-fee-replay test-genesis test-guarantor test-state-commitment-transition test-asset-registry test-daemon-lni-account exits 0; evidence: qual-logs/pay1/pay1d-item4-5-focused.log and pay1d-item4-5-focused.exit."
assumption = "The fee representation boundary in observations 3.7.28 and 3.7.30 is resolved by retaining version 1. A separate per-ordinal schedule is a governance follow-up outside this branch. Genesis materialization already registers the expanded Asset module; guarantor replay already dispatches the registered kernel implementation and needs no separate ordinal table."
severity = "note"

[observation.3.7.85]
task = "3.7"
file = "tests/test_state_commitment_transition.c tests/modules/test_asset_payloads.h tests/support/lxp_pay1_replay.h"
symbol = "pay1_submit_bytes pay1_receive_grant pay1_issuance pay1_snapshot_roundtrip pay1_malformed"
observed = "Signed kernel tests cover the seven new ordinals, replay, exact identity-sequence consumption, unchanged balances and module KV on refusals, and signed receipt root and endpoint tampering. Registration covers derived-id mismatch and duplicates; opening covers unknown and paused assets and duplicates; mint and burn cover unknown assets and accounts, asset mismatch, unauthorized actors, paused assets, frozen accounts, zero amount, cap exhaustion, exact cap, full burn and underflow. Grant issue covers invalid maximum, allowance, expiration, recurrence/window, recipient, purpose, identifier and signature, foreign key and owner, unknown asset/account, pause and duplicates. Receive covers missing grants, unknown assets/accounts, draw bounds, purpose, sequence, context, receiver network/controller/key/signature, idempotency binding, self draw, zero amount, pause, embedded grant mismatch, expiry, total and recurring exhaustion, invoice reuse and revocation. Revoke covers unknown grants, stale sequence, duplicate revocation and foreign owner. Canonical decoder prefix, trailing-byte, version, length and field bounds remain covered. Issued assets and grant state round-trip through real snapshots with identical state roots and account ids, assets, balances and sequences. Repeated issuance histories produce identical roots. make test-state-commitment-transition test-asset-registry test-asset-balance test-asset-transfer test-ledger-accounts test-ledger-receive test-ledger-receipt test-genesis test-guarantor and sh tools/lxp_check_sole_writer.sh exit 0; evidence: qual-logs/pay1/pay1d-item5-focused.log and pay1d-item5-sole-writer.log with adjacent exit files. Final additional owner and pause cases pass make test-state-commitment-transition; evidence: qual-logs/pay1/pay1d-item5-final-kernel.log and pay1d-item5-final-kernel.exit."
assumption = "Snapshot account ordering is canonical rather than insertion order; round-trip equality is checked by canonical account identity. Existing checks and protocol bounds remain unchanged."
severity = "note"

