symbol = "RpcClient Wallet wait_for WalletRpc"
observed = "The OpenRPC document defines eleven positional methods, including submission and three commitment selectors. Rust and TypeScript clients implement those methods and preserve JSON-RPC errors. The upstream public-core reference supplies exact sequence, receipt, inclusion and CP1/CX1 checkpoint result encodings. Wallet execution obtains independent identity and source sequences, binds full disclosure, uses the external signer and requires verified receipt evidence after submission. Batched verification checks the configured sequencer and Merkle inclusion. Finalised verification additionally pins the trusted context digest and verifies the exact CP1/CX1 certificate and matching header. The TypeScript wallet binding executes the real Rust wallet binary with an external signer socket."
assumption = "The contract omits lx_estimateFee, lx_listAssets and lx_getAsset; lx_getBalances still returns unavailable until native DID enumeration exists. Fee ceilings and finality trust inputs remain explicit configuration. Live public-RPC wallet execution was not exercised against an integrated gateway endpoint."
