observed = "Both Cargo lockfiles now contain only the packages and dependency disambiguation required by the workspace's pinned tungstenite dependency; locked hosted service builds and 37 gateway tests pass. A real TLS Redis 7.0.15 executable was installed at /usr/bin/redis-server and its system service is disabled and inactive. The local harness uses its existing certificate generator and an isolated TLS Redis process. The added disposable-custody fixture funds both principals, signs canonical Asset grant and Receive activities with real keys, requires executed and batched commitments, rejects ack, verifies receipts and batch inclusion, checks replay without a second debit, and records draw latency only after twenty successful draws. Strict standalone Clippy passes. Runtime reaches the real gateway after both custody credits, but platform/hosted/core/src/main.rs submission_registry registers only Asset ordinal 5; the gateway forwards ordinal 7 to /v1/activities and core returns invalid_activity before native admission. No draw executes and no p50 or p99 is claimed. Evidence: qual-logs/pay6/pay6f-redis-install.log, pay6f-redis-disable.log, pay6f-redis-state.log, pay6f-hosted-service-build.log, pay6f-gateway-tests.log, pay6f-hosted-clippy-rerun.log and pay6f-hosted-grant-draw-renewal-receipt-retry.log."
assumption = "The hosted core registry must admit the native Asset grant and Receive ordinals without bypassing canonical decoding. That core path is outside this lane's ownership. Cluster, image, deployed endpoint and production gates remain unrun."
severity = "blocker"

