observed = "Authenticated hosted admission strictly decodes Asset register, account_open, send, receive, grant_issue, grant_revoke, mint and burn, and Programs deploy, upgrade, call, transfer, account registration and wind-down. Asset ordinal 9 has a dedicated reserved-operation refusal and is excluded from execution admission. Every admitted type retains the SEND signer, fee-limit, native submission and receipt path. Fee estimates validate the same type set before using the authenticated committed native schedule. Three focused admission tests pass, including malformed payloads and the reserved ordinal. The disposable funded committed-read test prices all fourteen admitted types and returns the reserved refusal. Native state-commitment transition qualification executes the Asset operations with real state and native payload encoders. Strict core and gateway all-target Clippy and strict local-harness Clippy pass. Evidence: qual-logs/pay4/l/core-admission-tests-final.log, committed-fees-all-ordinals-publish.log, native-state-commitment-transition.log, platform-clippy-final.log and local-clippy-final.log."
assumption = "The authenticated committed schedule currently prices canonical bytes and the named SEND operation while execution and storage rates are zero. A future nonzero runtime-metered schedule remains fail closed until those units are supplied from authenticated execution facts."
severity = "note"

