observed = "ruff check agent/sdk/python exits 1 with 103 diagnostics across 38 files, led by 31 I001, 13 UP035, 11 B009, 7 PYI026, 6 TRY004, 6 PYI034 and 6 PYI001. No ruff.toml, no .ruff.toml and no tool.ruff section exists in agent/sdk/python/pyproject.toml, anywhere else in the tree or in the user configuration, so the rule set is whatever the installed release selects by default; the run recorded here used ruff 0.16.6. Thirty of the 38 files are byte-identical to 0717c87ca and carry 87 of the diagnostics. The remaining eight, the six x402 modules together with layerx_sdk/__init__.py and its stub, are byte-identical to f89cb11c0 and carry 16. No file differs from both sides. The test run in the same tree passes 34 tests once agent/sdk/python is on the interpreter path, which pytest does not arrange when the suite is invoked by path from the repository root. Evidence: qual-logs/rebase-205-11a.log and qual-logs/rebase-205-11b.log."
assumption = "Pinning a ruff version or adding a rule selection would decide a policy the SDK has never stated, and formatting the sources would rewrite files owned by another lane alongside this branch's own, so neither a configuration nor a formatter run was introduced. The interpreter path is supplied in the gate command."
