symbol = "GUARANTOR_COUNT settlement_document certificate_threshold metadata"
observed = "Both refusals recorded against the treasury boundary tests are closed at this revision and the suite runs fourteen of fourteen cases green (qual-logs/signer-test.log). Observation 6.1.4801 recorded that the genesis request length assertion in platform/hosted/node/bootstrap.sh expected 395 bytes plus metadata while the script emits 81 bytes per guarantor, so the repository settlement document's certificate_threshold of 2 refused; that assertion now reads 314 + 81 * GUARANTOR_COUNT + metadata and the script generates one secp256k1 guarantor key per guarantor, so platform/hosted/node/tests/signer-test.py passes contracts/config/checkpoint-settlement.json unmodified and asserts the threshold it carries is above one. Observation 6.1.4807 recorded that tests/support/lxgb_metadata.py emitted an asset record with custody_kind 1 against issuer_kind 2 and no custody reference, which issuer_valid refuses, so layerx-genesis-build refused every request built from it and the two end-to-end bootstrap cases failed; the fixture now emits the accepted shape and both cases build genesis, register the treasury identity and prove no copy of the seed survives."
assumption = "This supersedes observations 6.1.4801 and 6.1.4807. Neither bound nor fixture was changed from this row: both were corrected elsewhere on main and are byte-identical to origin/main on this branch. Before the fixture landed, the same result was obtained by correcting only the record shape in the working tree and restoring the file byte for byte (qual-logs/signer-test-with-g12-fixture.log); that probe is superseded by the run above against the shipped fixture."
severity = "note"

