observed = "Reconciling this transport branch onto the merged public-read, state-proven account read and asset work retired several of its hunks in favour of the branch-independent versions already published: the asset:<hex>:issuance account name shape, which lx_asset_issuance_name now only hashes as a seed while storing the name module:asset:value:<hex> and lx_account_migrate_retired_issuance migrates the old records; the gateway rpc.rs, ws.rs, public_reads.rs and openrpc.json duplicates, which are byte-identical on both sides; the pre-withdraw asset ordinal disclosure path; the smaller MCP tool catalogue; and the hosted core boundary fixture, which pins the V1_4 handshake and does not propagate LAYERX_PAY_TIMING through its spawn helper. The multi-asset offer, grant-draw module KV state and commitment additions of this branch are what survive the reconciliation."
assumption = "Every retired hunk has a branch-independent equivalent already published, so nothing was weakened to reconcile them. The boundary fixture handshake version and the LAYERX_PAY_TIMING propagation belong to the hosted-core owners rather than to this transport row."
severity = "note"

[observation.6.7.6609]
task = "6.7"
file = "agent/sdk/python/layerx_sdk/x402_draw.py platform/middleware/conformance/pay6/test_draw.py"
symbol = "PreparedGrantDraws._resolve _DrawUnresolved test_only_typed_protocol_pending_is_retryable"
observed = "The published Python SDK carried a lint-only refactor that routed every non-PaymentRpcError exception raised while resolving a prepared grant draw into a private _DrawUnresolved marker and answered None, which conflates transport, HTTP and parse failures with a protocol pending. test_only_typed_protocol_pending_is_retryable requires HTTPError and json.JSONDecodeError to propagate and requires only a JSON-RPC -32001 carrying an object data whose state is pending to answer None. The reconciliation keeps the extracted _resolve helper so the cleared lint finding stays cleared and moves the classification to its caller; the marker class became unreachable and was removed with it."
assumption = "The lint refactor preserved a pre-existing swallow rather than choosing it, so keeping its structure and adopting the typed classification satisfies both. No assertion was relaxed: the retryable case narrowed from any exception to the typed pending refusal."
severity = "note"

[observation.6.7.6610]
task = "6.7"
file = "agent/crates/layerx-agent-api/build.rs agent/crates/layerx-agent-api/src/generated.rs agent/schema/agent-api/v1.kvx"
symbol = "agent_api_compat_gate generated Rust contract drift"
observed = "Every agent-workspace cargo invocation fails in the layerx-agent-api build script: build.rs line 374 asserts that the committed src/generated.rs equals the text the generator emits from agent/schema/agent-api/v1.kvx, and the two differ only in the line wrapping of the format! call inside agent_api_compat_gate. The committed file carries the rustfmt-wrapped form and the generator emits the single-line form, so cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets and cargo test --workspace both exit 101 before compiling any crate. Evidence qual-logs/rebase-207-7.log and qual-logs/rebase-207-8.log. Neither the schema, the generator nor the generated file is touched by this transport branch; both are byte-identical to the published tree."
assumption = "The generator and the formatter disagree about the emitted text. Reconciling them belongs to the agent-api contract owners: either the generator emits the wrapped form or the check compares formatted text. Nothing here was regenerated, because the file is declared not hand-editable and regenerating it would silently change a published contract artefact."
severity = "blocker"

