[observation.6.8.167]
task = "6.8"
file = "platform/hosted/internal/src/events.rs"
symbol = "Observe Service::observe Service::route principal_matches derive"
observed = "formerly observation.6.8.6918. formerly observation.6.8.33. formerly observation.6.8.24. formerly observation.6.8.20. formerly observation.6.8.5. The observation POST contract is exactly {principal:string,resource:string} with deny_unknown_fields; it does not accept Fact or Record bodies. POST /internal/v1/observe requires peer_verified and the single configured bearer token. Service::observe binds the provisioned principal credential using GET /internal/v1/principal, then fetches the current resource through its existing route. Human journeys and approvals require active=true and sub equal to the original principal with Cookie __Host-layerx_access; payments and programs require principal_digest equal to SHA256 of the original principal with Authorization LayerX-Key. Every upstream response must be HTTP 200 application/json with ok=true and a result. Journey GET /v1/journeys/{resource} requires journey_id equal to resource and kind,state,updated_at; approval GET /v1/approvals/{resource} requires approval_id and agent_id,state,created_at; program GET /v1/programs/registry/{resource} requires program_id and top-level lifecycle,version,code_hash,receipt_digest. Fact names and values are strings; non-string upstream values are JSON encoded. Payment GET /v1/receipts/{resource} requires activity_id and a decodable protocol receipt whose activity matches resource, deriving activity_id,amount,asset and occurred_at from that receipt. Record is exactly id,principal,subject,subject_sequence,occurred_at,facts:[{name,value}], with optional activity_id,amount,asset. Identity is SHA256 of serialized principal,resource,current snapshot; the journal deduplicates that identity and assigns increasing sequence per principal and subject. GET /internal/v1/events/{64hex-id} reads one record and rebinds its stored principal. No kind-list route or caller-principal filter exists. Readiness probes the upstream, every credential binding and journal writability. Raw source excerpts: qual-logs/r24/event-contract.txt."
assumption = "The existing authenticated resource-derived contract must be reconciled explicitly before adding producers that require immutable transition payloads, stable retry identity or principal-filtered kind reads."
severity = "note"

[observation.6.8.168]
task = "6.8"
file = "platform/hosted/webhooks/src/trusted.rs"
symbol = "TrustedSources::fetch TrustedSources::event settled_payment internal_route Dashboard::receipt"
observed = "formerly observation.6.8.6919. formerly observation.6.8.34. formerly observation.6.8.25. formerly observation.6.8.21. formerly observation.6.8.6. TrustedSources fetches GET /internal/v1/events/{id} from one of four configured source Services and parses the exact Record fields with deny_unknown_fields and at most 32 facts. Non-payment facts become unverified; optional activity_id triggers independent component and authority verification. Payment always requires activity_id,amount,asset and settled_payment, which refuses missing receipt bytes, nonzero result code or evidence below receipt-verified. Thus accepted submissions without receipts and terminal refusals cannot be represented by the current payment consumer. Webhook ingestion requires POST /internal/v1/events/{singular-kind}/{source-event-id} with the source-trigger bearer; posting observe alone does not call HostedService::publish. Dashboard reads HostedReader Redis shards by principal, not the internal sources. PaymentView reads state,amount,asset and only reports settled with a receipt-verified state fact and digest; Dashboard::receipt additionally requires matching receipt-backed activity_id. No journey or approval event projection exists in Dashboard service.rs. The sink hashes the latest fetched snapshot rather than a producer transition identity, so a lost observe response followed by a state change can make a retry append a different record and delayed delivery can collapse intermediate transitions. Gateway submit_activity handles admission at main.rs:1773; complete_activity persists verified terminal data at main.rs:1960. KeyRecord contains principal_digest without the original principal required by the sink, so passing it as principal would hash twice and fail binding. Registry registry_read_json returns latest_version,versions[].code_hash and receipt.deployment_receipt_digest, not the top-level fields derive requires. Its raw deployment ingress deliberately refuses untrusted caller proof bytes. These conflicts remain unchanged. Raw source excerpts: qual-logs/r24/event-contract.txt."
assumption = "Consumer changes require ownership of webhooks/src/trusted.rs and events.rs; accepted and refused payments need explicit non-settlement contracts preserving every existing settlement check. Immutable retry semantics require a durable transition identifier and authenticated historical resource reads. A raw-principal provisioning map must be explicit, never inferred by reversing a digest."
severity = "blocker"

