observed = "The failing Receive path in observation 3.7.9982 remains a production codec conflict. LxpReceive emits tag 0x5201 with eight fields and carries only a grant identifier; PayerGrantRoute also stores only the identifier and sequence, key and context. The existing native-compatible payment/disclosure decoder requires the ten-field, 733-byte Receive envelope containing both the canonical signed Grant and ReceiverAuthorization. The old producer cannot satisfy this strict decoder. At revision 65878e1c48bda59e894cdb9cbdc3fe94999d1ee0, command cargo test --locked --manifest-path human/Cargo.toml -p layerx-human-service --test binding --test custody --test journey_faults --test move_money --test reclaim --test render --test session_keys --test withdraw --test archive --no-fail-fast -- --test-threads=2 exited 101 with 39 passes and the same two Receive preparation failures. The full integrated workspace run reproduced both failures."
assumption = "The strict decoder, legacy producer and both existing failing assertions remain intact. Closing this requires the actual signed payer-grant and receiver authorization inputs, versioned durable route encoding, explicit refusal of unsigned legacy routes and real issuer/receiver caller integration. This source conflict is not solved by replacing test values or loosening preparation. Exact focused failed output remains in qual-logs/q10-human-fixture-tests.*."
severity = "blocker"

